WORK ROOT: /Users/aelaguiz/workspace/codex-client ; UPSTREAM: /Users/aelaguiz/workspace/codex

ALREADY-KNOWN DRAFT LOCATIONS (verify line numbers, classify action, and FIND WHAT IS MISSING — your main value is completeness):
- Swift order: DockSessionTable.swift (sessionsByID dict ~24, sortedSessions ~257-270), DockSessionProjection.swift (rowPrecedesByRecency ~349-360, pinnedRowPrecedes ~362-382), ArchiveSessionProjector.swift (~39-55), PinnedMetadataOrdering.
- Swift projection/build: DockRenderProjector.swift (~50-67), SessionSummaryMapper.swift (~48-106), SessionRowProjector.swift (activityMode ~12, ~99-141), DockModels.swift (DockRowViewModel ~179-243), SessionSummary type, LocalThreadMetadataStore.swift (LocalPinnedDisplaySnapshot ~43-109), DockScreenStore.swift, DockView.swift.
- Wire DTO: CodexDock/AppServer/DockStreamDTO.swift (~222-352), ThreadListDTO.swift, AppServerMethods.swift, AppServerDockStreamClient.swift, AppServerDockClient.swift (legacy direct path).
- Relay: scripts/dock-relay-state-views.mjs (normalizeThread ~242-270, normalizeStoredSession ~272-295, orderedDockRows ~211-240, buildWindow ~315-325, boundedText), dock-relay-state-store.mjs (listDockSessions/ORDER BY ~340, applyDockReconciliation ~453-513, dock_order), dock-relay-state-engine.mjs, dock-relay-state-subscriptions.mjs (dockDelta, schemaVersion literal), dock-relay-state-snapshot.mjs, dock-relay-constants.mjs, dock-relay.mjs (JSON-RPC wiring), dock-relay-thread-summary-cache.mjs, dock-relay-thread-data.mjs (legacy).
- Tests: CodexDockTests/DockStoreTestSupport.swift (~257-275, ~789-846 fixtures that set message fields), DockStoreStreamTests.swift, ResponsivenessContractTests.swift, RenderCoalescerTests.swift, scripts/dock-relay-state-parity.mjs (~2746 single-window stop), scripts/dock-relay-state-snapshot.test.mjs.
- Upstream: codex/codex-rs/app-server-protocol/.../v2/thread_data.rs (seconds), thread_processor.rs (~3944-3945 .timestamp()), state/src/runtime/threads.rs (ms allocator).`

phase('Enumerate')

const TASKS = [
  {
    label: 'swift-order-projection',
    bucket_hint: 'must-touch-production',
    task: `Enumerate EXHAUSTIVELY every Swift location that (a) sorts/orders/compares rows (search for: .sorted, sort(by, "precedes", "Precedes", "rowPrecedes", "<" comparators on rows, "orderKey", "lastActivityDate", "messageActivityDate"), (b) builds a domain/row model from a DTO (SessionSummary, DockRowViewModel, any "Mapper"/"Projector"/"summary(from:")), or (c) reads messageUpdatedAt / messageSummary / activityMode / lastActivity / messageActivityDate. For each: exact path + symbol + line range, and classify action (change | retire | keep-verbatim) under the decided architecture. Explicitly state for each ordering/projection site whether it serves Dock, Archive, Detail, or Pinned — and whether it must collapse into the single orderKey comparator + single card->viewmodel mapping. Flag any site I did not list in the draft.`
  },
  {
    label: 'wire-contract-both-sides',
    bucket_hint: 'must-touch-production',
    task: `Enumerate EXHAUSTIVELY the wire-contract surface on BOTH languages for the schema-as-source change. (1) Swift: every file/struct/field of the Dock stream DTO family (DockStreamSessionDTO, DockStreamUpdateDTO, window/freshness/host sub-structs), every decode/encode/CodingKeys site, the schemaVersion constant (CodexDockConstants.Dock.streamSchemaVersion), and where a GENERATED Swift card struct would land. (2) Relay Node: every .mjs function that constructs or serializes the wire row/envelope object (normalizeThread, normalizeStoredSession, dockDelta, makeSnapshot, makeDelta, buildWindow, sequenceFields), every schemaVersion literal, and where a Node schema-VALIDATOR would hook in. (3) Identify the natural home for the single schema artifact (note: upstream codex uses app-server-protocol/schema/typescript/v2/ as a generated-schema pattern — is there an analogous home here or must a new contract dir be created?). For each: path + symbol/line + action + which side. Flag anything missing from the draft.`
  },
  {
    label: 'tests-fixtures-hidden-consumers',
    bucket_hint: 'must-touch-tests',
    task: `Two jobs. (1) Enumerate EVERY test file, fixture builder, and harness that touches the ordering/card contract: anything that SETS messageSummary or messageUpdatedAt (grep both, in CodexDockTests and scripts), anything that asserts row ORDER, the stream-lifecycle tests, and the parity harness (confirm the exact single-subscribe/stop location and what it would take to consume dock/update catch-up to complete:true). Classify each (change | retire | add). (2) HUNT for hidden NON-test production consumers of messageUpdatedAt, messageSummary, SessionSummary, SessionSummaryMapper, and the legacy direct thread/list Dock path (AppServerDockClient) anywhere in the app — anything that would break or need migration when these are retired/changed. Also list the exact test commands (npm test:relay, swift test --filter ...). Flag anything missing from the draft.`
  },
  {
    label: 'docs-config-not-touch',
    bucket_hint: 'docs-runbook',
    task: `Three jobs. (1) Enumerate EVERY docs/ file that states the Dock row/order/summary/status/identity contract and would need updating or a pointer when the DockThreadCard contract lands (search docs/ for the row contract, ordering rules, status taxonomy, the relay state engine architecture doc, the responsiveness doc, README sections, and the existing root-cause worklog). For each: path + which section + why it is affected. (2) Enumerate any CONFIG/SERVICE/launch surfaces affected by a schema version bump or new contract: relay startup/port wiring, launchd/plist or run scripts, any place schemaVersion must be coordinated across deploy, package.json scripts, Swift build config for a codegen step. (3) Confirm the DO-NOT-TOUCH set: list the specific files/subsystems that are correct and must be preserved verbatim (RenderCoalescer + its tests, off-main projection wiring, lazy detail fetch ThreadDetailStore + ThreadDetailRenderProjector + ThreadEvent pipeline, the bounded windowed envelope mechanics, relay byte/row bounding + incremental diff), with a one-line reason each. Flag anything missing.`
  },
]

const results = await parallel(TASKS.map(t => () =>
  agent(CONTEXT + '\n\n## YOUR ENUMERATION ASSIGNMENT (' + t.label + ', primary bucket: ' + t.bucket_hint + '):\n\n' + t.task, { label: t.label, phase: 'Enumerate', schema: ENTRY_SCHEMA })
))

return results.filter(Boolean)

